  "ab.st_build": "This page was built at {t} from code {sha}",
  "ab.h_tabs": "What each tab is for and how to read it",
  "ab.tab.survival": "The first screen. Guides for not over-reaching in the current market: the risk ceiling (danger signal), candidates, virtual positions (machine assumptions), a ruin-probability estimate, and the notification and verification logs. All are assumptions or summaries, not real trading results.",
  "ab.tab.nikkei225": "Nikkei 225 constituents. Each row shows the chart signal (buy, sell, …) next to that signal's past record (verification). Click a row for the detail chart: close, Bollinger Bands and CCI. Fair value, value quintile and overall grade exist only in the Mac mini version; the public site has no values for them.",
  "ab.tab.dow30": "Dow Jones (30 stocks). Read it like Nikkei 225 (chart signal + verification + detail chart).",
  "ab.tab.nasdaq100": "Nasdaq 100. Same reading. Above the table is a combined list of buy signals across the three US indexes (Dow, Nasdaq 100, S&P 500).",
  "ab.tab.sp500": "S&P 500. Same reading. When fewer constituents than the target were fetched, the tab name shows the actual count.",
  "ab.tab.fx": "FX, commodities and crypto. The overall direction (LONG to SHORT) and where CCI and the Bollinger Bands stand. The stock chart-signal verification is not applied to FX.",
  "ab.tab.rates_vol": "Interest rates (US, Japan and euro-area government bond yields) and equity/rate volatility (VIX etc.). The shape of the yield curve is macro context.",
  "ab.tab.pos_val": "Speculative positioning (CFTC futures positions, weekly) and a whole-market valuation gauge (Buffett Indicator). Both are long-horizon context, not trade signals.",
  "ab.tab.relations": "The yield-equity balance: whether stocks and bonds move together or opposite, how sensitive each index is to rate moves, and an estimate of rebalancing pressure.",
  "ab.tab.moneyflow": "An animation of where money is flowing in three regions (US, Europe, Japan), with a cross-asset correlation panel below.",
  "ab.tab.verify": "How prices actually moved after past stock chart signals and composite scores (return after a fixed number of trading days), compared with the same stock's all-period average (the base). If recent results fall below the base, the site shows “evidence is weakening”.",
  "ab.tab.about": "This page: the purpose of each tab, how to read the indicators, the rules, update times, data status and limitations.",
  "ab.h_chart": "Chart signal rules (the “signal” column on stock tabs)",
  "ab.chart_intro": "Computed every day from daily high, low and close. Stocks with fewer than {min} daily bars get no signal. Checked from the top; the first match is the day's signal.",
  "ab.cond_cci": "CCI{n} {op} {v}",
