  "ab.cci_spike": "“Mass break”: a day when the count of {ev} exceeds the larger of the top {top}% of daily counts over the past {days} trading days and {frac}% of the market's stocks (a possible crash marker). Not judged with less than {min} days of history.",
  "ab.h_ind": "How to read the indicators",
  "ab.ind_cci": "Commodity Channel Index: how far the average of high, low and close is from its recent mean. CCI{l} (long) above 0 means the long trend is up, below 0 down. CCI{s} (short) below −{th} suggests short-term oversold, above +{th} overbought.",
  "ab.ind_bb": "Bollinger Bands: mean ± standard deviation. Uses ±{k2}σ and ±{k3}σ of BB{s} (short) and BB{l} (long). Below −{k2}σ means far below the mean. The composite score's BB% is the position inside the BB{n} band.",
  "ab.ind_rsi": "Relative Strength Index ({n} days): gains versus losses on a 0–100 scale. Lower suggests oversold, higher overbought.",
  "ab.ind_macd": "Difference between short and long exponential averages ({f} and {s} days, signal {g} days). A positive histogram means upward momentum.",
  "ab.ind_ema": "Exponential moving averages ({a}, {b}, {c} days). The more the close sits above them in order, the stronger the uptrend.",
  "ab.ind_atr": "Average True Range ({n} days): the typical daily range. Larger means rougher price moves. Useful for stop distance and position size (not used in any signal).",
  "ab.ind_score_name": "Composite score",
